Hi again Mark,

> 1. I think you have to specify the yearlySiteCovs:
>
> ammaMF <- formatLong(amma, type = "unmarkedMultFrame", numPrimary = 5, yearlySiteCovs = visit)

Please see Dan Linden's nice description of these types of covariates <https://groups.google.com/d/msg/unmarked/TrZD8Oxj-OM/AkZQSeZZwZMJ>. A yearlySiteCov is a variable the varies among sites in a given year, and within a site(s) over multiple years.

None of your covariates fits this description and, as such, you do not have any yearlySiteCovs.

FWCPdata <- read.csv("~/FWS_Projects/sandbox/Data/FWCPDataLongTsp.csv", header = TRUE, stringsAsFactors = FALSE) %>%
  # Drop records with no response; we'll complete data set below
  filter(!is.na <http://is.na>(y))

# Explore covariate temporal variation within sites
cov_temp <- group_by(FWCPdata, site) %>%
  summarise_at(vars(place.1, vri.2, wetdist.3, cutdist.4, rddist.5), n_distinct)
summary(cov_temp)
#>      site              place.1      vri.2     wetdist.3   cutdist.4
#>  Length:103         Min.   :1   Min.   :1   Min.   :1   Min.   :1.000
#>  Class :character   1st Qu.:1   1st Qu.:1   1st Qu.:1   1st Qu.:1.000
#>  Mode  :character   Median :1   Median :1   Median :1   Median :1.000
#>                     Mean   :1   Mean   :1   Mean   :1   Mean   :1.049
#>                     3rd Qu.:1   3rd Qu.:1   3rd Qu.:1   3rd Qu.:1.000
#>                     Max.   :1   Max.   :1   Max.   :1   Max.   :2.000
#>     rddist.5
#>  Min.   :1
#>  1st Qu.:1
#>  Median :1
#>  Mean   :1
#>  3rd Qu.:1
#>  Max.   :1

This summary does highlight why `cutdist.4` is being treated as an obsCov rather than a siteCov. There must be a few sites that have different values within a site within a year, likely some kind of data entry error based on your surprise at it being treated different than you other siteCovs.

Sure enough, looks like `cutdist.4` values change within a handful of sites:

# What's up with cutdist.4?
weird_cutdist <- filter(cov_temp, cutdist.4 > 1) %>% pull(site)
filter(FWCPdata, site %in% weird_cutdist, spp.6 == "amma") %>%
  mutate(date = dmy(date)) %>% # Convert string to date)
  arrange(site, spp.6, date)
#>    site       date y y.count place.1 vri.2 wetdist.3 cutdist.4 rddist.5
#> 1  p.44 2014-05-13 0       0       p    TC     42.96    779.07   295.73
